WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.936
This is pre-Katniss.
-Set 64 years in the past.

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:06.506
It's been 10 years
since the districts

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:09.108
and The Capitol
have, like, gone to war.

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.477
And the Hunger Games have been
going on for 10 years.

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:13.513
-It's a giant,
giant, giant movie.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:17.850 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.286 line:0%
Viola Davis,
welcome back to the show.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.222 line:0%
-Thank you.
Every time someone stands up,

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.157 line:0%
I'm like,
"Do you really know who I am?"

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.692 line:0%
-Yes! Absolutely!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:29.762 line:0%
We love you! Come on.
-I'll accept it.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.130
-Last time you were
on our show --

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.331
I feel like
we're good luck together,

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:33.833
'cause last time
you were on the show,

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.035
you were promoting
"The Woman King."

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.404
-Yes.
-And you were like, "Jimmy,

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:39.872
I worked so hard
on this thing."

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:41.907
Backstage. And you're like,
"I'm just nervous.

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:43.576
I'm excited about this.
I think it's a great movie.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.211
I want people to go out there
and see it."

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.146
And not only did people
go out and see it,

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.514
it was the number-1 movie

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:51.484
and then one of
the best films of 2022.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.887
[ Cheers and applause ]
Viola Davis crushed it!

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.755
You were awesome!
-Thank you, thank you.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:59.526
-You were awesome!
-I was the O.G. warrior.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:02.328
-You were fantastic.
That was great.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:06.031
And then, since I've seen you,
you won a Grammy Award,

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:07.367
and -- I know, but --

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.469
Come on.

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:13.873
For a recording of
the audiobook of your

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.775
number-1 best-selling book,
"Finding Me."

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.076
-Yes.
-Come on.

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:22.082
This is -- It's all happening.
It's all happening.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.317
But then it put you
in EGOT status.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.385
-Yes.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:28.087
-Emmy, Grammy, Oscar, Tony --
EGOT.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.756
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:33.193
-I think I can retire now.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:35.995
-Never! Don't you ever retire.
Are you kidding me? We need you.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.464
-Why not? Why can't I retire?
-Never.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:39.498
-I can do whatever I want.
-No!

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:41.300
-I'm an EGOT.
-I know.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.802
[ Laughs ] Exactly.

00:01:43.802 --> 00:01:47.073
Did it -- How does it feel?
Are you excited?

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.708
Do you even look at it
and process it yet?

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.443
-No, I don't look at it.
-You don't.

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:52.578
-I don't --
-I would.

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.246
-You know what? That's a lie.

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:57.449
I just told a bold-faced lie
on national television.

00:01:57.449 --> 00:01:59.185
-You look at all of them?

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.520
-No, as soon as I got
that Grammy in the mail,

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.025
I put that Grammy, that Tony,
that Oscar, that Emmy,

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.894
and I took a fabulous picture.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:10.295
-That's exactly -- Yes!

00:02:10.295 --> 00:02:14.566
Something. You got to enjoy it
because you earned it

00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:15.601
and you got it.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.503
-That's right.
-That is so cool.

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:18.972
Maybe next time you come on,
maybe I can --

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.440
We could see
if you can bring it with you.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.408
But that's a lot of awards.
-No, I'm not going to do that.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:25.545
-I know. Yeah, I know.
I understand, I understand.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:28.948
I want to talk to you about
the new "Hunger Games" movie.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.016
-Yes.
-This comes out --

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.384
We can talk about movies.
-Okay.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.118
-Actors can talk about movies.
-Finally!

00:02:33.118 --> 00:02:36.922
-Yes! It feels great.

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:38.891
Look at you, by the way.

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.159
Look at Viola Davis.
-Yeah, uh-huh.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:43.429
-Look at this. Can we...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.733
"Hunger Games: The Ballad
of Songbirds and Snakes."

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:49.469
This is the origin story.
-This is the origin story.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.437
I feel like every character
I do now

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:54.707
is an homage to my childhood,

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:58.211
which means that I don't want
anyone messing with me.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.012
I want to kick people's ass.

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:02.882
-What are you talking --
What are you talking about?

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.050
That's --

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.051
-I mean,
it's like a villain in this,

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:07.787
a warrior in "Woman King."

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:11.190
You know, everything is about,
"I'm gonna kick somebody's ass!"

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:14.193
-This is different sides
of you that we like to --

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:15.595
Do you like playing the villain?

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:16.962
-Oh, I love
playing the villain

00:03:16.962 --> 00:03:18.731
because everybody sees me.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.934
Everybody wants to hug me.
Everybody wants to kiss me.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.569
There are grown men
who want to kiss me

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.571
in the parking lot of Target.

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:28.374
You know, they want to --
they want to hold me.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:31.377
And literally, they come up to
me and I'm thinking,

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.979
"Okay, they're going to ask me
for an autograph or whatever."

00:03:33.979 --> 00:03:35.815
Sometimes, they have tears
in their eyes,

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.750
and they're like,
"Can I hug you?"

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:38.951
-Yeah.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:41.287
-You know, almost like
they have to reconcile

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.655
a bad childhood or something.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:45.190
And I always hug them.
-You do?

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:49.061
But now --
But those days are over.

00:03:49.061 --> 00:03:50.196
Those days are over now.

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.597
-No, I'm still gonna
hug them,

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:54.566
because, you know, really,
really, at the end of the day,

00:03:54.566 --> 00:03:56.068
I like when people
stand up for me.

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:57.837
-Yeah, I know you do.
Yeah, I know you love it.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:00.940
But I like that you play
different roles

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.374
and you could play
whatever you want to do.

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:05.444
And this looks like fun to me.
-And we shot it in Berlin.

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:08.748
And let me tell you something --
It -- I'll tell you --

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:12.217
my experience in Berlin
can be summed up in one thing.

00:04:12.217 --> 00:04:16.689
When I came back to Los Angeles,
my triglycerides were high.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:17.823
-Okay.

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:19.525
-That was my experience
in Berlin.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.195
-Just ate.
-I ate, I drank.

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:25.030
I got in that Jacuzzi every day.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.834
And let me tell you something,
I love a Jacuzzi.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.803
I love a Jacuzzi.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.571
And when I got
in that Jacuzzi --

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:37.176
my $10 bathing suit -- I got
in that Jacuzzi every night.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:42.314
I was invited to the opera by
random strangers in the Jacuzzi.

00:04:42.314 --> 00:04:43.750
-Wait, wait, wait, wait.
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.386
-I was invited to dinner from
random strangers in the Jacuzzi.

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:49.622
I got a whole skin line --

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:52.658
skincare line from someone
who sat in the Jacuzzi.

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:55.861
They recognized me and said,
"Oh, you know what?

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:58.363
I have a whole skincare line
that I want to give you."

00:04:58.363 --> 00:05:00.599
-Wait, no. Viola Davis,
I have to ask you this question.

00:05:00.599 --> 00:05:02.668
I'm sorry. Rewind.
We missed a big thing here.

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:06.472
You went to, like,
a public Jacuzzi?

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:09.942
-That's all you got
from that story?

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:12.211
-Yes.
You won every award you can.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:14.413
-What other Jacuzzi
am I going to go to?

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:16.082
-I thought maybe you had
a private Jacuzzi.

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.717
I wouldn't --
You went to, like, a --

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.318
-Well, you need to call
the producers

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:20.620
of "Hunger Games" about that.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.754
I did not have the suite
with the private Jacuzzi.

00:05:22.754 --> 00:05:25.457
-So, it's a hotel,
and you're at the hotel Jacuzzi.

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:29.962
-Listen, I looked at the back
of a hairy man's red ass.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:34.667
-What is going on?
What is going on at this hotel?

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.403
-Yes.
-But you went back.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:40.306
-I went back.
Listen, I got a skincare line.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:44.176
I got invited to the opera.
I got invited to dinner.

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:46.779
I was -- And, literally,
I would tell my friends

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.547
Jamika and Sergio --
I was like,

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:50.449
"You want to come
to Jacuzzi with me?

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:54.920
I got invited to the opera.
We have a skincare line.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.322
You don't want to look
at the back of that man's ass."

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:57.423
-No, no, no.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.659
But you always have
the memories.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:00.893
-Yes.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.862
-But that's insane
that you would do that.

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.697
Did people freak out
and go like,

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.298
"I'm in a Jacuzzi
with Viola Davis"?

00:06:06.298 --> 00:06:08.834
-No, I don't --
Here's the thing.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:13.105
I'm just going to say it.
I got to show my I.D. a lot.

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:15.374
There's not a lot of people
who recognize me.

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:17.777
Well, there was some times
they recognize me.

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:22.248
Sometimes, they think I'm Oprah.
They think I'm Alfre Woodard.

00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:24.416
You know, they think
I'm Taraji P. Henson,

00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:26.085
which really baffles me.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.519
-Wow!
-You know?

00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:31.156
-That's insane.
I just love that you do that.

00:06:31.156 --> 00:06:35.294
-Yes, absolutely.
You work out in the gym.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:39.164
Walked in the park in Germany
late at night

00:06:39.164 --> 00:06:40.599
with all my friends.

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:42.234
And as soon as
it got really dark,

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:44.604
I'm thinking, "Oh, my God.

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:46.805
It is dark.
It's in the park.

00:06:46.805 --> 00:06:48.874
Somebody's going to get us."
-Yeah.

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:52.945
-I walked in that park
with a straight up tree limb.

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:56.515
-As a weapon?
-As a weapon.

00:06:56.515 --> 00:07:00.252
-What is going on at this hotel?
-I live my best life.

00:07:00.252 --> 00:07:03.456
-You never had to use
the tree limb, though, did you?

00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:05.424
Yeah, maybe? Okay.
Alright, alright.

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:08.294
-I would never say
if I used a tree limb.

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:09.729
-Is this because of all these

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:10.830
action movies
that you're doing now?

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:11.964
You're getting
this new Viola Davis?

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:13.432
-Yeah, I think so.

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:17.636
And, you know, the the makeup in
"Hunger Games" took four hours.

00:07:17.636 --> 00:07:18.638
-I know. That's what
I was saying.

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:20.473
Could we zoom in?
-Four hours.

00:07:20.473 --> 00:07:24.277
And then it took maybe
45 minutes to take it off.

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:27.779
And the hardest part to take off
was the nose.

00:07:27.779 --> 00:07:30.983
I mean, it was so hard
that the makeup artists

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:35.854
literally had to brace
their feet and just pull it.

00:07:35.854 --> 00:07:39.125
It was like an anal probe.

00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:42.795
It was like --
I mean, stretching it.

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:44.630
-What?!
-You have no idea.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:49.301
I said -- It was like -- I mean,
plastic that was coming out.

00:07:49.301 --> 00:07:52.738
By that point,
we were hysterical.

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:55.407
-But do you like getting into
character that deep

00:07:55.407 --> 00:07:57.442
and going like, "Oh, I can go as
crazy as I want.

00:07:57.442 --> 00:07:58.878
I can go to a next level."

00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:02.815
-Absolutely, because I always
want people to see me different.

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:03.949
-Yeah.

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:06.485
-You know -- Now, I love
when people love me.

00:08:06.485 --> 00:08:10.689
I love when people see me
as maternal and warm and fuzzy.

00:08:10.689 --> 00:08:13.392
But there are times when I just
want to scare the

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:15.194
[bleep] out of them.

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:16.628
-Oh, my God.

00:08:16.628 --> 00:08:19.665
Okay, there's this Viola,
and there's this Viola.

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:20.833
-Yeah.
-Okay, good.

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:22.735
-I like her.
-Yeah, yeah, we do.

00:08:22.735 --> 00:08:25.804
We like her, too.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:25.804 --> 00:08:28.006
We love you.
I want to show a clip.

00:08:28.006 --> 00:08:30.443
Here's Viola Davis in
"The Hunger Games:

00:08:30.443 --> 00:08:32.511
The Ballad of
Songbirds and Snakes."

00:08:32.511 --> 00:08:33.746
Take a look at this origin...

00:08:33.746 --> 00:08:35.181
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:42.988
How tantalizing to see
all your shining young faces

00:08:42.988 --> 00:08:45.824
on this auspicious day.

00:08:45.824 --> 00:08:49.995
I am Dr. Volumnia Gaul,
your humble head gamemaker,

00:08:49.995 --> 00:08:56.368
in charge of the War Department
and all its affiliated concerns.

00:08:56.368 --> 00:09:01.607
I've broken free of my
laboratory today to examine you,

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:05.077
the leaders
of the next generation.

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:08.547
I won't be around forever,
after all.

00:09:08.547 --> 00:09:09.881
[ Laughs ]

00:09:09.881 --> 00:09:12.551
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:14.520
I have things I want
to ask about you.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:17.756 line:0%
One is your name -- Rachel.
-Yes.

00:09:17.756 --> 00:09:20.826 line:0%
-You got this -- You got your
name from someone very famous.

00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:22.995 line:0%
And am I right?
-You are correct.

00:09:22.995 --> 00:09:25.131 line:0%
I was named after
Rachel Green from "Friends."

00:09:25.131 --> 00:09:27.399
-Okay, good. Alright.
That is real?

00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:29.302
-That is real.
That is a real fact.

00:09:29.302 --> 00:09:31.503
And everybody --
Nobody ever believes me

00:09:31.503 --> 00:09:33.839
because they think
that there's no way

00:09:33.839 --> 00:09:36.075
I'm young enough
to be named after "Friends."

00:09:36.075 --> 00:09:37.243
But --
-No, you were.

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:38.511
-But I am, yeah.

00:09:38.511 --> 00:09:40.412
My mom -- They were
going to name me Catherine,

00:09:40.412 --> 00:09:42.447
but my older sister's
Jacqueline, and they thought

00:09:42.447 --> 00:09:44.816
that might be too confusing
for babies to figure out.

00:09:44.816 --> 00:09:46.352
-Yeah. Catherine and Jacqueline.
Yeah.

00:09:46.352 --> 00:09:49.521
-Yeah. And, so, yeah,
my mom loved the way it sounded

00:09:49.521 --> 00:09:51.423
on "Friends"
for Jennifer Aniston,

00:09:51.423 --> 00:09:53.158
and then that was my name.

00:09:53.158 --> 00:09:55.560
-I mean, that's a perfect
person to be named --

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.663
We love -- Who doesn't love
Jennifer Aniston or Rachel?

00:09:57.663 --> 00:09:58.897
-I love Jennifer.

00:09:58.897 --> 00:10:00.565
-You could have been
named after the hairstyle.

00:10:00.565 --> 00:10:04.103
-I could have been Ross.
-You could have been Ross.

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:05.471
-Who knows?
-You could have been Ross.

00:10:05.471 --> 00:10:06.705
Yeah, alright.
-All right, why not, right?

00:10:06.705 --> 00:10:07.773
-Ross Zegler's got a good name
to it, as well.

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:08.874
-Yeah, right?

00:10:08.874 --> 00:10:12.177
-Well, if you want to have
a brother...

00:10:12.177 --> 00:10:13.511
I want to talk to you
about this,

00:10:13.511 --> 00:10:15.447
because I know you're a big --
You're a big Swiftie.

00:10:15.447 --> 00:10:16.849
-Yes.
-And you were at the...

00:10:16.849 --> 00:10:18.783
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:18.783 --> 00:10:20.152
I mean, how cool are you?

00:10:20.152 --> 00:10:21.353
-She looks very sad,

00:10:21.353 --> 00:10:23.889
but that was just
because I had food poisoning.

00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:25.257
-No.
-I did.

00:10:25.257 --> 00:10:26.525
-You did not.
-I did.

